\layout Subsection*

Average number in System.
\layout Standard

The average number of calls in the Erlang Delay System
\layout Standard


\begin_inset Formula \[
\bar{N}=\frac{\rho }{1-\rho }C(m,a)+m\rho \]

\end_inset 

 These terms represent the average queue length and the average number of
 busy lines.
 
\begin_inset Formula \[
\bar{N}_{Q}=\frac{\rho }{1-\rho }C(m,a)\]

\end_inset 

 So the average waiting time is simply 
\begin_inset Formula \[
\bar{W}=\frac{\bar{N}_{Q}}{\lambda }=\frac{C(m,a)}{m\mu (1-\rho )}\]

\end_inset 


\layout Example*

So what is the average waiting time for the telephone service centre example?
 
\layout Standard


\begin_inset Formula $m=8$
\end_inset 

, 
\begin_inset Formula $\mu =\frac{1}{8}$
\end_inset 

, 
\begin_inset Formula $\rho =\frac{\lambda }{m\mu }=\frac{1}{2}$
\end_inset 

.
 
\layout Standard

delay is 
\begin_inset Formula $\frac{0.1}{8\frac{1}{8}(1-\frac{1}{2})}=0.2$
\end_inset 

 minutes, or 12 seconds.
 
